{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of a two-sheet implication in the aligned nontrivial cubic-Kummer analysis at actual partial degrees (6,9). Every field-valued solution of the four lower-Pfaffian invariant equations is proved to lie on a common-power sheet with zero source bracket or on an elliptic sheet; converse inclusions and existence of the sheets are not compared.  The formalization derives the elliptic equation and terminal one-form, excludes nonconstant reduced rational trajectories on its C != 0 fibre by a finite forbidden-value argument, factors the C=0 fibre, and verifies the shifted Davenport--Stothers bracket, terminal descent, infinity arithmetic, and one-root cube conclusion.  It does not formalize the remaining finite-place valuation classification and therefore does not claim the full noncube branch, all (6,9), maximum eleven, or JC2.",
